diff --git a/android/app/src/main/assets/licenses/win-fg-NOTICE.md.txt b/android/app/src/main/assets/licenses/win-fg-NOTICE.md.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..876d8c5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/android/app/src/main/assets/licenses/win-fg-NOTICE.md.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Win-FG optical flow in Dragon Rage opt3
+
+Source: https://github.com/The412Banner/win-fg
+Pinned commit: fbc69ed6c5bf16b824d0a29bd8b171675101f9dd (2026-10-29 retrieval).
+License: MIT, copyright 2026 The412Banner; see LICENSE and the AMD notice.
+
+Derived shaders: of3_luma, of3_downsample, of3_flow_m4, of3_expand_m4,
+wfg_synth, renamed fg_luma/down/flow/expand/synth. Original copyright and
+algorithm attribution comments are retained. No Lossless.dll, learned weights,
+proprietary LSFG shaders or binaries are included. This is not LSFG itself.
+
+Changes: SDL_GPU resource sets, image graph and synchronization; bounded
+working resolution; correct per-axis pyramid scaling for non-power-of-two
+sizes; subpixel refinement at the actual finest level with unbiased SAD;
+endpoint forward/backward consistency; half-resolution confidence fields;
+GPU scene-cut reduction; optional upper 18% HUD exclusion; pair reuse for
+2x/3x/4x synthesis; 5x5 matching support and an independent zero-centred
+search hypothesis to recover from coarse-level aliasing. Full global-affine and TV-L1 passes are not enabled.
+
+The cut detector and SDL C integration are new Dragon Rage code. An output
+candidate may contain original pixels where confidence is low or a cut/HUD
+guard activates. Generated presentation count is not a simulation FPS metric.
diff --git a/android/app/src/main/assets/licenses/win-fg-NOTICE_FIDELITYFX_OPTICALFLOW.md.txt b/android/app/src/main/assets/licenses/win-fg-NOTICE_FIDELITYFX_OPTICALFLOW.md.txt
